        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\n\nYes, this is intentional to have zoomed and non-zoomed views be visually different. If users want to have the same highlight, adding window-local `winhighlight` in the zoomed window is indeed one way to do it. For example, like this:\n\n```lua\nlocal my_zoom = function()\n  MiniMisc.zoom()\n  -- Differentiate between zooming in (floating window) and zooming out (not floating window)\n  -- This is not 100% solution, but should work for 99% of cases\n  if vim.api.nvim_win_get_config(0).relative == '' then return end\n  vim.wo.winhighlight = 'NormalFloat:Normal'\nend\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<Leader>z', my_zoom, { desc = 'Zoom' })\n```\n\nClosing as working as expected.",
